@* Two empty <template> markers delimit this scope for WssEditControls.focusFirstField, and they are
   rendered ONLY while FocusFirstField resolves true -- the default-off render tree is byte-identical
   to what this component emitted before the feature existed. <template> is the least intrusive
   element available: the UA stylesheet gives it display:none (no layout box, no flex/grid item), it
   has no accessibility presence, and its content model is inert. It is still an ELEMENT, so a
   consumer stylesheet that counts children of whatever contains <FormDefaults> (:first-child,
   :nth-child, :only-child) sees two more of them -- which is the trade the opt-in buys. *@
@if (_focusScopeId is not null)
{
    <template id="@_focusScopeId"></template>
}
<CascadingValue TValue="FormDefaults" Value="this" IsFixed="true">@ChildContent</CascadingValue>
@if (_focusScopeId is not null)
{
    <template id="@(_focusScopeId + FocusScopeEndSuffix)"></template>
}
